# Cloudflare Pages redirects — https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Only the admin entry needs a rule: the URL the studio types (/admin, /admin/)
# is rewritten to the second Vite entry, admin.html. Pages applies these rules
# BEFORE it looks for a static asset, so a "/* /index.html 200" catch-all
# would have proxied every request — hashed JS/CSS chunks, images,
# robots.txt — to index.html and broken the site on first deploy. It is not
# needed: with no 404.html in the build, Pages already serves index.html for
# any path that matches no asset, which is exactly the SPA fallback the
# react-router routes need.
/admin    /admin.html   200
/admin/    /admin.html   200

# Prerendered per-route files are flat (stories/<slug>.html served at
# /stories/<slug>); send the trailing-slash form to the canonical URL rather
# than relying on undocumented normalisation.
/stories/:slug/    /stories/:slug    301
/more/:slug/       /more/:slug       301
